-- 5-player dungeon spawns Legends of Azeroth Pandaria 5.4.8 has and SkyFire lacks (GPL v2, world DB of 2024-07-22).
-- Creatures: skyfire_port_plan/tools/SpawnFill.pl; gameobjects: tools/GoFill.py. For each entry LoA spawns more often
-- on a map, same-entry spawns are paired one to one by distance and the unpaired LoA spawns are added, unless any
-- SkyFire spawn stands within 4 yards; waypoint paths (id guid*10) and per-spawn addons come along.
-- Left out: LoA spawns in a pool, a game event or a phase other than 1, and every entry that map's SkyFire scripts
-- name in a Summon call, reference in their code, or summon through SmartAI / creature_summon_groups (found with
-- tools/summoned.py), so nothing is doubled: e.g. the Ring of Law beasts and Theldren (BRD), Gyth (UBRS),
-- Krik'thir's swarmers, Ick's passenger Krick and Tyrannus' Icy Blasts (PoS), the Culling's zombies and Chromie,
-- the Halls of Reflection escort, the ToC 5-player champions and chests, Tuten'kash's tomb fiends, the Zul'Farrak
-- pyramid bosses, Gnomeregan's rockets, Eck's Ruins Dwellers.
-- Computed against world_dev with the open dungeon PRs applied (#206, #210, #212, #214).
-- GUID block 9692000+ (creatures 9692000-9693321, gameobjects 9692000-9692390). No database names; safe to run twice.

